{"chunk_id": "b54bcba49564", "text": "Sage Valmiki asks the divine sage Narada whether a perfect man exists\u2014one who embodies virtue, courage, wisdom, truth, and compassion. Narada answers by recounting the life of Rama of the Ikshvaku line, describing his noble qualities and the great events of his life. He summarizes Rama\u2019s exile due to Queen Kaikeyi\u2019s demand, the loyal companionship of Sita and Lakshmana, and King Dasaratha\u2019s death. In the forest Rama slays demons and later forms an alliance with the monkey king Sugriva after killing Bali. The search for Sita leads Hanuman to leap to Lanka, find her, and burn the city. Rama builds a bridge across the sea, defeats Ravana, proves Sita\u2019s purity through the fire ordeal, and returns to rule Ayodhya in a just and prosperous reign\u2014establishing the ideal of righteous kingship.\nNarada tells Valmiki the life story of Rama\u2014from virtues and exile to Sita\u2019s abduction, Ravana\u2019s defeat, and Rama\u2019s just rule in Ayodhya.\nThemes: ideal kingship, dharma and obedience, exile and devotion, good versus evil, divine incarnation", "vector": [0.008645310066640377, -0.017778608947992325, -0.009990575723350048, -0.006113045383244753, -0.013624112121760845, 0.014428634196519852, -0.018556753173470497, -0.010986336506903172, -0.029754111543297768, -0.00948280468583107, 0.010168625973165035, 0.00998398195952177, 0.0032164379954338074, 0.01781817525625229, -0.014257178641855717, -0.0032642476726323366, 0.04339141398668289, -0.01209420245140791, 0.019216196611523628, -0.009219027124345303, -0.007306639105081558, -0.01996796391904354, -0.009370698593556881, 0.0014334663283079863, -0.019545918330550194, -0.0011935936054214835, 0.027089959010481834, -0.028830889612436295, 0.032260000705718994, -0.01328120194375515, -0.0098520927131176, -0.01599811017513275, -0.0060207233764231205, -0.00017392834706697613, -0.023146484047174454, 0.021181339398026466, -0.012146958149969578, 0.008823360316455364, 0.0